---
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---

<section class="relative overflow-hidden">
  <div class="absolute inset-0 -z-10">
    <div class="absolute left-1/2 top-0 h-[700px] w-[700px] -translate-x-1/2 -translate-y-1/2 rounded-full bg-primary-500/10 blur-3xl dark:bg-primary-500/5"></div>
    <div class="absolute right-0 top-1/3 h-[400px] w-[400px] rounded-full bg-primary-400/10 blur-3xl dark:bg-primary-400/5"></div>
  </div>

  <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-6 pb-24 pt-24 sm:pt-36">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-4xl text-center">

      <div class="mb-6 inline-flex items-center gap-2 rounded-full border border-primary-200 bg-primary-50 px-4 py-1.5 text-sm font-semibold text-primary-700 dark:border-primary-800/50 dark:bg-primary-900/20 dark:text-primary-400">
        <span class="h-1.5 w-1.5 rounded-full bg-primary-500"></span>
         No vendor lock-in - Works in any AI IDE, Claude Code, Cursor or GitHub Copilot
      </div>

      <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-zinc-900 dark:text-white">
        Meet Baxter, the Agentic BA !
      </h1>

      <p class="mx-auto mt-8 max-w-2xl text-base leading-relaxed text-zinc-600 dark:text-zinc-400">
        Your AI business analyst — essentially an open source AI Harness that works alongside you to craft and verify business requirements, change requests, bug reports, and other artefacts against your real codebase, right inside the AI coding IDE you already use, with support for markdown and version control.
      </p>

      <div class="mt-12 flex justify-center">
        <a href={`${base}getting-started/`} class="inline-flex items-center justify-center rounded-lg bg-primary-600 px-8 py-4 text-base font-semibold text-white shadow-sm transition-all hover:bg-primary-700 hover:shadow-md">
          Get Started with Baxter
          <svg class="ml-2 h-5 w-5" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke-width="2" stroke="currentColor">
            <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M13.5 4.5L21 12m0 0l-7.5 7.5M21 12H3" />
          </svg>
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
